{"slug":"/students/subjects/english/core-grammar/tense-aspect/","source":"students/subjects/english/core-grammar/tense-aspect.html","area":"students","kind":"content","title":"Tense & Aspect — Core Grammar","description":"","subject":"english","body":"<div class=\"max-w-4xl mx-auto\">\n    <nav class=\"mb-4\"><a href=\"/students/subjects/english/core-grammar/\" class=\"text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800\">← Back to Core Grammar</a></nav>\n    \n    <article class=\"card p-6 rounded-lg mb-6\">\n      <h1 class=\"text-3xl font-bold mb-2 text-gray-800\">Tense &amp; Aspect</h1>\n      <p class=\"text-gray-600 mb-6\">Master the twelve English tenses and their aspects to express time relationships accurately in your writing and speech. This is a crucial topic in WAEC English Language examinations.</p>\n      \n      <!-- Learning Objectives -->\n      <div class=\"bg-blue-50 border-l-4 border-blue-500 p-4 mb-6 rounded-r\">\n        <h2 class=\"font-semibold text-blue-800 mb-2\">📚 Learning Objectives</h2>\n        <ul class=\"list-disc pl-5 text-gray-700 space-y-1\">\n          <li>Understand the difference between tense (time) and aspect (nature of action)</li>\n          <li>Learn all 12 English tenses with their forms and uses</li>\n          <li>Identify and correct common tense errors</li>\n          <li>Apply correct tenses in WAEC-style questions</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div>\n    </article>\n\n    <!-- Section 1: Understanding Tense vs Aspect -->\n    <section class=\"card p-6 rounded-lg mb-6\">\n      <h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center gap-2\">\n        <span class=\"bg-indigo-100 text-indigo-800 px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-sm\">1</span>\n        Tense vs Aspect\n      </h2>\n      \n      <div class=\"grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-4\">\n        <div class=\"bg-blue-50 p-4 rounded-lg\">\n          <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-blue-800 mb-2\">⏰ Tense</h3>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm\">Indicates <strong>when</strong> an action happens - past, present, or future.</p>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mt-2\">Example: \"She <strong>went</strong>\" (past) vs \"She <strong>goes</strong>\" (present)</p>\n        </div>\n        \n        <div class=\"bg-green-50 p-4 rounded-lg\">\n          <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-green-800 mb-2\">🔄 Aspect</h3>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm\">Indicates <strong>how</strong> an action occurs - simple, continuous, perfect, or perfect continuous.</p>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mt-2\">Example: \"She <strong>wrote</strong>\" (simple) vs \"She <strong>was writing</strong>\" (continuous)</p>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"bg-amber-50 border-l-4 border-amber-500 p-4 rounded-r\">\n        <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-amber-800 mb-2\">💡 Key Concept</h4>\n        <p class=\"text-gray-700\">Combining 3 tenses × 4 aspects gives us <strong>12 English tenses</strong>. Mastering these will significantly improve your grammar accuracy in WAEC exams.</p>\n      </div>\n    </section>\n\n    <!-- Section 2: Present Tenses -->\n    <section class=\"card p-6 rounded-lg mb-6\">\n      <h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center gap-2\">\n        <span class=\"bg-green-100 text-green-800 px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-sm\">2</span>\n        Present Tenses\n      </h2>\n      \n      <div class=\"space-y-4\">\n        <!-- Present Simple -->\n        <div class=\"bg-green-50 p-4 rounded-lg\">\n          <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-green-800 mb-2\">Present Simple</h3>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mb-2\"><strong>Form:</strong> Base verb (add s/es for third person singular)</p>\n          <div class=\"bg-white p-3 rounded mb-2\">\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700\"><strong>Examples:</strong></p>\n            <ul class=\"list-disc pl-5 text-gray-600 text-sm\">\n              <li>I <strong>study</strong> English every day.</li>\n              <li>She <strong>teaches</strong> at the secondary school.</li>\n              <li>The sun <strong>rises</strong> in the east.</li>\n            </ul>\n          </div>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm\"><strong>Uses:</strong> Habits, facts, general truths, scheduled events</p>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Present Continuous -->\n        <div class=\"bg-teal-50 p-4 rounded-lg\">\n          <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-teal-800 mb-2\">Present Continuous</h3>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mb-2\"><strong>Form:</strong> am/is/are + verb-ing</p>\n          <div class=\"bg-white p-3 rounded mb-2\">\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700\"><strong>Examples:</strong></p>\n            <ul class=\"list-disc pl-5 text-gray-600 text-sm\">\n              <li>She <strong>is reading</strong> a newspaper now.</li>\n              <li>They <strong>are playing</strong> football outside.</li>\n              <li>I <strong>am writing</strong> an essay.</li>\n            </ul>\n          </div>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm\"><strong>Uses:</strong> Actions happening now, temporary situations, future plans</p>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Present Perfect -->\n        <div class=\"bg-emerald-50 p-4 rounded-lg\">\n          <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-emerald-800 mb-2\">Present Perfect</h3>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mb-2\"><strong>Form:</strong> have/has + past participle</p>\n          <div class=\"bg-white p-3 rounded mb-2\">\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700\"><strong>Examples:</strong></p>\n            <ul class=\"list-disc pl-5 text-gray-600 text-sm\">\n              <li>I <strong>have finished</strong> my homework.</li>\n              <li>She <strong>has visited</strong> Ghana twice.</li>\n              <li>They <strong>have lived</strong> here for ten years.</li>\n            </ul>\n          </div>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm\"><strong>Uses:</strong> Completed actions with present relevance, experiences, actions starting in past and continuing</p>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Present Perfect Continuous -->\n        <div class=\"bg-cyan-50 p-4 rounded-lg\">\n          <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-cyan-800 mb-2\">Present Perfect Continuous</h3>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mb-2\"><strong>Form:</strong> have/has been + verb-ing</p>\n          <div class=\"bg-white p-3 rounded mb-2\">\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700\"><strong>Examples:</strong></p>\n            <ul class=\"list-disc pl-5 text-gray-600 text-sm\">\n              <li>She <strong>has been studying</strong> for three hours.</li>\n              <li>They <strong>have been waiting</strong> since morning.</li>\n              <li>It <strong>has been raining</strong> all week.</li>\n            </ul>\n          </div>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm\"><strong>Uses:</strong> Actions continuing from past to present, emphasizing duration</p>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </section>\n\n    <!-- Section 3: Past Tenses -->\n    <section class=\"card p-6 rounded-lg mb-6\">\n      <h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center gap-2\">\n        <span class=\"bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-sm\">3</span>\n        Past Tenses\n      </h2>\n      \n      <div class=\"space-y-4\">\n        <!-- Past Simple -->\n        <div class=\"bg-orange-50 p-4 rounded-lg\">\n          <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-orange-800 mb-2\">Past Simple</h3>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mb-2\"><strong>Form:</strong> Verb + ed (regular) or irregular form</p>\n          <div class=\"bg-white p-3 rounded mb-2\">\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700\"><strong>Examples:</strong></p>\n            <ul class=\"list-disc pl-5 text-gray-600 text-sm\">\n              <li>I <strong>visited</strong> my grandmother yesterday.</li>\n              <li>She <strong>wrote</strong> a letter last week.</li>\n              <li>Nigeria <strong>gained</strong> independence in 1960.</li>\n            </ul>\n          </div>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm\"><strong>Uses:</strong> Completed actions at a specific time in the past</p>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Past Continuous -->\n        <div class=\"bg-amber-50 p-4 rounded-lg\">\n          <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-amber-800 mb-2\">Past Continuous</h3>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mb-2\"><strong>Form:</strong> was/were + verb-ing</p>\n          <div class=\"bg-white p-3 rounded mb-2\">\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700\"><strong>Examples:</strong></p>\n            <ul class=\"list-disc pl-5 text-gray-600 text-sm\">\n              <li>She <strong>was cooking</strong> when I arrived.</li>\n              <li>They <strong>were playing</strong> football at 5 PM.</li>\n              <li>While he <strong>was reading</strong>, she <strong>was writing</strong>.</li>\n            </ul>\n          </div>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm\"><strong>Uses:</strong> Actions in progress at a specific past time, interrupted actions</p>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Past Perfect -->\n        <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg\">\n          <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-yellow-800 mb-2\">Past Perfect</h3>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mb-2\"><strong>Form:</strong> had + past participle</p>\n          <div class=\"bg-white p-3 rounded mb-2\">\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700\"><strong>Examples:</strong></p>\n            <ul class=\"list-disc pl-5 text-gray-600 text-sm\">\n              <li>She <strong>had left</strong> before I arrived.</li>\n              <li>By the time the police came, the thief <strong>had escaped</strong>.</li>\n              <li>I realized I <strong>had forgotten</strong> my keys.</li>\n            </ul>\n          </div>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm\"><strong>Uses:</strong> Actions completed before another past action (the \"past of the past\")</p>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Past Perfect Continuous -->\n        <div class=\"bg-stone-50 p-4 rounded-lg\">\n          <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-stone-800 mb-2\">Past Perfect Continuous</h3>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mb-2\"><strong>Form:</strong> had been + verb-ing</p>\n          <div class=\"bg-white p-3 rounded mb-2\">\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700\"><strong>Examples:</strong></p>\n            <ul class=\"list-disc pl-5 text-gray-600 text-sm\">\n              <li>She <strong>had been waiting</strong> for two hours when he finally came.</li>\n              <li>They <strong>had been living</strong> in Lagos before they moved to Abuja.</li>\n            </ul>\n          </div>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm\"><strong>Uses:</strong> Actions continuing up to a point in the past</p>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </section>\n\n    <!-- Section 4: Future Tenses -->\n    <section class=\"card p-6 rounded-lg mb-6\">\n      <h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center gap-2\">\n        <span class=\"bg-purple-100 text-purple-800 px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-sm\">4</span>\n        Future Tenses\n      </h2>\n      \n      <div class=\"space-y-4\">\n        <!-- Future Simple -->\n        <div class=\"bg-purple-50 p-4 rounded-lg\">\n          <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-purple-800 mb-2\">Future Simple</h3>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mb-2\"><strong>Form:</strong> will + base verb</p>\n          <div class=\"bg-white p-3 rounded mb-2\">\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700\"><strong>Examples:</strong></p>\n            <ul class=\"list-disc pl-5 text-gray-600 text-sm\">\n              <li>I <strong>will visit</strong> my parents next weekend.</li>\n              <li>She <strong>will be</strong> eighteen next month.</li>\n              <li>The examination <strong>will begin</strong> on Monday.</li>\n            </ul>\n          </div>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm\"><strong>Uses:</strong> Predictions, promises, decisions made at the moment, future facts</p>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Future Continuous -->\n        <div class=\"bg-violet-50 p-4 rounded-lg\">\n          <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-violet-800 mb-2\">Future Continuous</h3>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mb-2\"><strong>Form:</strong> will be + verb-ing</p>\n          <div class=\"bg-white p-3 rounded mb-2\">\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700\"><strong>Examples:</strong></p>\n            <ul class=\"list-disc pl-5 text-gray-600 text-sm\">\n              <li>This time tomorrow, I <strong>will be traveling</strong> to Kano.</li>\n              <li>She <strong>will be sleeping</strong> when you arrive.</li>\n            </ul>\n          </div>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm\"><strong>Uses:</strong> Actions in progress at a specific future time</p>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Future Perfect -->\n        <div class=\"bg-fuchsia-50 p-4 rounded-lg\">\n          <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-fuchsia-800 mb-2\">Future Perfect</h3>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mb-2\"><strong>Form:</strong> will have + past participle</p>\n          <div class=\"bg-white p-3 rounded mb-2\">\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700\"><strong>Examples:</strong></p>\n            <ul class=\"list-disc pl-5 text-gray-600 text-sm\">\n              <li>By next year, I <strong>will have graduated</strong>.</li>\n              <li>She <strong>will have finished</strong> the project by Friday.</li>\n            </ul>\n          </div>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm\"><strong>Uses:</strong> Actions completed before a specific future time</p>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Future Perfect Continuous -->\n        <div class=\"bg-pink-50 p-4 rounded-lg\">\n          <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-pink-800 mb-2\">Future Perfect Continuous</h3>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mb-2\"><strong>Form:</strong> will have been + verb-ing</p>\n          <div class=\"bg-white p-3 rounded mb-2\">\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700\"><strong>Examples:</strong></p>\n            <ul class=\"list-disc pl-5 text-gray-600 text-sm\">\n              <li>By December, I <strong>will have been studying</strong> English for five years.</li>\n              <li>She <strong>will have been working</strong> here for ten years next month.</li>\n            </ul>\n          </div>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm\"><strong>Uses:</strong> Duration of an action up to a specific future time</p>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </section>\n\n    <!-- Tense Summary Table -->\n    <section class=\"card p-6 rounded-lg mb-6\">\n      <h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-4\">📊 Tense Summary Chart</h2>\n      \n      <div class=\"overflow-x-auto\">\n        <table class=\"w-full text-sm border-collapse\">\n          <thead class=\"bg-gray-100\">\n            <tr>\n              <th class=\"border p-2 text-left\">Tense/Aspect</th>\n              <th class=\"border p-2 text-left\">Simple</th>\n              <th class=\"border p-2 text-left\">Continuous</th>\n              <th class=\"border p-2 text-left\">Perfect</th>\n              <th class=\"border p-2 text-left\">Perfect Cont.</th>\n            </tr>\n          </thead>\n          <tbody>\n            <tr>\n              <td class=\"border p-2 font-semibold\">Present</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">I work</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">I am working</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">I have worked</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">I have been working</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr class=\"bg-gray-50\">\n              <td class=\"border p-2 font-semibold\">Past</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">I worked</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">I was working</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">I had worked</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">I had been working</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr>\n              <td class=\"border p-2 font-semibold\">Future</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">I will work</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">I will be working</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">I will have worked</td>\n              <td class=\"border p-2\">I will have been working</td>\n            </tr>\n          </tbody>\n        </table>\n      </div>\n    </section>\n\n    <!-- WAEC Worked Examples -->\n    <section class=\"card p-6 rounded-lg mb-6\">\n      <h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-4\">📝 WAEC-Style Worked Examples</h2>\n      \n      <div class=\"space-y-4\">\n        <div class=\"bg-blue-50 p-4 rounded-lg\">\n          <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-blue-800 mb-2\">Example 1: Present vs Past</h4>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-2\"><strong>Question:</strong> Fill in the blank with the correct tense:</p>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-2\">\"She ______ (study) English for three years now.\"</p>\n          <div class=\"mt-3 text-green-700\">\n            <strong>Solution:</strong> \"She <strong>has been studying</strong> English for three years now.\"<br>\n            <span class=\"text-sm\">The phrase \"for three years now\" indicates an action that started in the past and continues to the present, requiring Present Perfect Continuous.</span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"bg-orange-50 p-4 rounded-lg\">\n          <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-orange-800 mb-2\">Example 2: Past Perfect</h4>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-2\"><strong>Question:</strong> Choose the correct verb form:</p>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-2\">\"By the time we arrived, the train ______ (leave).\"</p>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700\">A. left B. had left C. has left D. was leaving</p>\n          <div class=\"mt-3 text-green-700\">\n            <strong>Solution:</strong> B. <strong>had left</strong><br>\n            <span class=\"text-sm\">The Past Perfect is needed because the train left BEFORE we arrived. Both are in the past, but one happened before the other.</span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"bg-purple-50 p-4 rounded-lg\">\n          <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-purple-800 mb-2\">Example 3: Future Perfect</h4>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-2\"><strong>Question:</strong> Rewrite using the Future Perfect tense:</p>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-2\">\"She completes the project by next week.\"</p>\n          <div class=\"mt-3 text-green-700\">\n            <strong>Solution:</strong> \"She <strong>will have completed</strong> the project by next week.\"<br>\n            <span class=\"text-sm\">\"By next week\" indicates completion before a future point, requiring Future Perfect.</span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </section>\n\n    <!-- Common Errors -->\n    <section class=\"card p-6 rounded-lg mb-6\">\n      <h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-4\">⚠️ Common Tense Errors</h2>\n      \n      <div class=\"space-y-3\">\n        <div class=\"bg-red-50 p-3 rounded-lg\">\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700\"><span class=\"text-red-600\">❌ Incorrect:</span> \"I am understanding the lesson.\"</p>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700\"><span class=\"text-green-600\">✓ Correct:</span> \"I understand the lesson.\"</p>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-500 text-sm\">Stative verbs (understand, know, believe, like) are rarely used in continuous tenses.</p>\n        </div>\n        \n        <div class=\"bg-red-50 p-3 rounded-lg\">\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700\"><span class=\"text-red-600\">❌ Incorrect:</span> \"She has visited Lagos yesterday.\"</p>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700\"><span class=\"text-green-600\">✓ Correct:</span> \"She visited Lagos yesterday.\"</p>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-500 text-sm\">Specific past time expressions (yesterday, last week) require Past Simple, not Present Perfect.</p>\n        </div>\n        \n        <div class=\"bg-red-50 p-3 rounded-lg\">\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700\"><span class=\"text-red-600\">❌ Incorrect:</span> \"If I will see him, I will tell him.\"</p>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700\"><span class=\"text-green-600\">✓ Correct:</span> \"If I see him, I will tell him.\"</p>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-500 text-sm\">In time clauses (if, when, after, before), use Present Simple for future meaning.</p>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </section>\n\n    <!-- Practice Exercises -->\n    <section class=\"card p-6 rounded-lg mb-6\">\n      <h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-4\">🎯 Practice Exercises</h2>\n      \n      <div class=\"space-y-6\">\n        <div>\n          <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2\">Exercise A: Choose the Correct Tense</h4>\n          <ol class=\"list-decimal pl-5 space-y-2 text-gray-700\">\n            <li>By this time next year, I ______ (will graduate/will have graduated).</li>\n            <li>She ______ (has worked/has been working) here since 2020.</li>\n            <li>While I ______ (was walking/walked) home, it started to rain.</li>\n            <li>Nigeria ______ (became/has become) independent in 1960.</li>\n          </ol>\n        </div>\n\n        <div>\n          <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2\">Exercise B: Convert the Tense</h4>\n          <ol class=\"list-decimal pl-5 space-y-2 text-gray-700\">\n            <li>Convert to Present Continuous: \"She reads newspapers.\"</li>\n            <li>Convert to Past Perfect: \"He finished his work.\"</li>\n            <li>Convert to Future Continuous: \"I sleep at midnight.\"</li>\n          </ol>\n        </div>\n\n        <div>\n          <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2\">Exercise C: Error Correction</h4>\n          <ol class=\"list-decimal pl-5 space-y-2 text-gray-700\">\n            <li>Correct: \"I am knowing the answer.\"</li>\n            <li>Correct: \"She has arrived yesterday.\"</li>\n            <li>Correct: \"They are study English now.\"</li>\n          </ol>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <details class=\"mt-4 bg-green-50 p-4 rounded-lg cursor-pointer\">\n        <summary class=\"font-semibold text-green-800\">📋 View All Answers</summary>\n        <div class=\"mt-3 space-y-2 text-gray-700\">\n          <p><strong>Exercise A:</strong></p>\n          <p>1. will have graduated 2. has been working 3. was walking 4. became</p>\n          <p class=\"mt-2\"><strong>Exercise B:</strong></p>\n          <p>1. She is reading newspapers. 2. He had finished his work. 3. I will be sleeping at midnight.</p>\n          <p class=\"mt-2\"><strong>Exercise C:</strong></p>\n          <p>1. I know the answer. 2. She arrived yesterday. 3. They are studying English now.</p>\n        </div>\n      </details>\n    </section>\n\n    <!-- Video Resource -->\n    <section class=\"card p-6 rounded-lg mb-6\">\n      <h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-4\">📺 Video Lesson</h2>\n      <div class=\"aspect-video bg-gray-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden\">\n        <iframe class=\"w-full h-full\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/4IWgPumNk1g\" title=\"English Tenses Lesson\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture\" allowfullscreen=\"\">\n        </iframe>\n      </div>\n      <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-500 mt-2\">Video: All 12 English Tenses Explained</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <!-- Key Takeaways -->\n    <section class=\"card p-6 rounded-lg\">\n      <h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-4\">🔑 Key Takeaways</h2>\n      \n      <div class=\"grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4\">\n        <div class=\"bg-green-50 p-4 rounded-lg\">\n          <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-green-800 mb-2\">Present Tenses</h4>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm\">Use for current habits, facts, ongoing actions, and experiences with present relevance.</p>\n        </div>\n        \n        <div class=\"bg-orange-50 p-4 rounded-lg\">\n          <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-orange-800 mb-2\">Past Tenses</h4>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm\">Use for completed actions. Past Perfect shows the \"past of the past.\"</p>\n        </div>\n        \n        <div class=\"bg-purple-50 p-4 rounded-lg\">\n          <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-purple-800 mb-2\">Future Tenses</h4>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm\">Use for predictions, plans, and actions completed before a future point.</p>\n        </div>\n        \n        <div class=\"bg-blue-50 p-4 rounded-lg\">\n          <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-blue-800 mb-2\">Time Expressions</h4>\n          <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm\">Keywords like \"since,\" \"for,\" \"yesterday,\" \"by the time\" signal which tense to use.</p>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      \n      <div class=\"mt-4 p-4 bg-yellow-50 rounded-lg\">\n        <p class=\"text-gray-700\"><strong>💡 Exam Tip:</strong> Look for time markers in WAEC questions. Words like \"yesterday,\" \"for five years,\" \"by next week,\" and \"now\" are clues to the correct tense.</p>\n      </div>\n    </section>\n  </div>\n<!-- Topic Quiz System -->","bodyClass":"min-h-screen bg-gradient-to-br from-yellow-50 to-orange-100 p-6","bodyStyle":"","css":["body{font-family:Inter, sans-serif}.card{ -webkit-backdrop-filter:blur(12px);backdrop-filter:blur(12px);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.85);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.18);} details[open] summary{border-bottom:1px solid #e5e7eb;padding-bottom:8px;margin-bottom:12px;}"],"quiz":null,"tracker":null,"links":[]}